===== README.md =====
     1	# Relux Proxy
     2	
     3	Relux Proxy currently ships as a native macOS menu bar app that manages one SSH
     4	dynamic SOCKS5 tunnel. It uses the system `/usr/bin/ssh`, so hosts, keys, jump
     5	hosts, and other options from `~/.ssh/config` continue to work. The planned
     6	versioned contract for saved, concurrent legacy SOCKS tunnels is
     7	[`.spec/legacy-socks-multi-tunnel.md`](.spec/legacy-socks-multi-tunnel.md); it
     8	is not shipped behavior yet.
     9	
    10	The repository also contains the approved specifications and implementation
    11	backlog for a future macOS/iOS system VPN over SSH. That VPN is not implemented
    12	yet. Start with [the specification index](.spec/README.md),
    13	[the current-state inventory](docs/current-state.md), and
    14	[the saved task-board workflow](docs/project-management.md).
    15	
    16	## Use
    17	
    18	1. Open Relux Proxy from Applications.
    19	2. Enter an SSH-reachable IP address, hostname, or `~/.ssh/config` alias, an
    20	   optional account, and a local SOCKS port. Leave **Account** empty to let
    21	   system OpenSSH use the matching config's `User` (or its normal default). A
    22	   non-empty account is an explicit SSH user override.
    23	3. Choose **Connect**.
    24	4. In Firefox, open **Settings → Network Settings**, select **Manual proxy configuration**, and set:
    25	   - SOCKS Host: `127.0.0.1`
    26	   - Port: the port shown by Relux Proxy (`1080` by default)
    27	   - SOCKS v5
    28	   - Proxy DNS when using SOCKS v5
    29	
    30	The initial defaults are `administrator@relux` and `127.0.0.1:1080`.
    31	
    32	## Download
    33	
    34	The latest signed and notarized build always has the same asset name and URL
    35	(GitHub authentication is required while this repository is private):
    36	
    37	https://github.com/relux-works/relux-proxy/releases/latest/download/ReluxProxy.dmg
    38	
    39	Versioned DMGs and SHA-256 checksums are available on the GitHub Releases page.
    40	
    41	## Development
    42	
    43	Requirements: macOS 14 or newer and Xcode 15.3 or newer.
    44	
    45	```bash
    46	make test
    47	make app
    48	make run
    49	```
    50	
    51	### Development tools
    52	
    53	| Command | Purpose | Output or effect |
    54	| --- | --- | --- |
    55	| `make test` | Run the SwiftPM test suite. | SwiftPM build and test data in `.build/`. |
    56	| `make app` | Build and sign the macOS application. | `dist/ReluxProxy.app`. |
    57	| `make dmg` | Build the app, then package a disk image. | `dist/ReluxProxy-v<version>-universal.dmg`. |
    58	| `make run` | Build the app, then open it. | Opens `dist/ReluxProxy.app`. |
    59	
    60	The app is intentionally not sandboxed because it needs to launch the system SSH executable. Release bundles use the hardened runtime and are signed with the Relux Works Developer ID.
    61	
    62	Contributors must follow [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md). Planned VPN work is
    63	tracked in `.task-board/`; no VPN implementation should begin without explicit
    64	approval of the generated plan.
    65	
    66	## Release
    67	
    68	Push a semantic version tag to build, sign, notarize, staple, attest, and publish both versioned and stable-name DMGs:
    69	
    70	```bash
    71	git tag -s v0.1.0 -m "Relux Proxy v0.1.0"
    72	git push origin v0.1.0
    73	```
    74	
    75	The release workflow expects `MACOS_CERT_P12`, `ASC_KEY_ID`, `ASC_ISSUER_ID`, and `ASC_KEY_P8` repository secrets. `ASC_KEY_P8` and `MACOS_CERT_P12` are base64 encoded.
===== docs/current-state.md =====
     1	# Current state and migration boundary
     2	
     3	Last verified: 2026-07-28.
     4	
     5	## What exists
     6	
     7	The repository builds one SwiftPM macOS 14 executable, `ReluxProxy`, packaged by
     8	shell scripts as a menu bar `.app` and DMG.
     9	
    10	The app:
    11	
    12	- stores one SSH host, account, and local SOCKS port in the legacy
    13	  `AppStorage` keys `sshHost`, `sshAccount`, and `localPort`;
    14	- has one shared `TunnelController` and can therefore run only one SSH child
    15	  and one SOCKS tunnel at a time;
    16	- launches `/usr/bin/ssh -N -C -D 127.0.0.1:<port>` with fail-fast, keepalive,
    17	  timeout, batch-mode, and quiet logging options;
    18	- passes an empty account as the bare host target, allowing system OpenSSH to
    19	  use a matching `User` setting (or its normal default); a non-empty account is
    20	  sent as `account@host`, which is an explicit SSH user override;
    21	- accepts an IP address, hostname, or `Host` alias and lets the system client
    22	  apply matching `~/.ssh/config` behavior such as `HostName`, `Port`,
    23	  `IdentityFile`, and `ProxyJump`;
    24	- binds the SOCKS listener only to IPv4 loopback (`127.0.0.1`) and keeps a
    25	  trailing 4,000-character in-memory diagnostic for that one tunnel;
    26	- reports connecting, connected, disconnecting, disconnected, and failed states;
    27	- requires the user to configure a browser or other SOCKS-aware client manually;
    28	- intentionally runs outside the App Sandbox so it can spawn system SSH.
    29	
    30	Tests cover profile validation and exact SSH argument construction. CI runs
    31	`swift test` and builds an ad-hoc-signed universal application bundle.
    32	
    33	Tagged releases import the Relux Works Developer ID certificate, build a
    34	universal app, sign the DMG, notarize and staple it, validate it with Gatekeeper,
    35	publish checksums/provenance, and upload both versioned and stable
    36	`ReluxProxy.dmg` assets.
    37	
    38	## What does not exist
    39	
    40	The current app is not a system VPN and does not contain:
    41	
    42	- saved multi-profile configuration or concurrent SOCKS tunnels;
    43	- iOS targets;
    44	- `NETunnelProviderManager` or packet-tunnel extensions;
    45	- a userspace TCP/IP stack or packetFlow bridge;
    46	- an embedded SSH implementation;
    47	- UDP or system DNS forwarding;
    48	- the remote `relux-relay` executable/protocol;
    49	- shared profile/Keychain state between host and extension;
    50	- Network Extension entitlements or provisioning;
    51	- TestFlight/App Store release automation.
    52	
    53	## Migration boundary
    54	
    55	[the legacy SOCKS multi-tunnel contract](../.spec/legacy-socks-multi-tunnel.md)
    56	is the versioned implementation contract for a planned extension of this legacy
    57	macOS SOCKS mode. It defines the one-time migration of the three keys above,
    58	profile persistence, OpenSSH account precedence, port ownership, and
    59	independent multi-tunnel lifecycle. It does not claim that the current release
    60	already has those capabilities.
    61	
    62	The planned VPN product in `.spec/` remains a new architecture, not an
    63	incremental toggle inside `TunnelController`. Existing source files remain the
    64	current SOCKS product until board-approved migration tasks create the
    65	multi-target project.
    66	
    67	During migration:
    68	
