===== README.md =====
     1	# Relux Proxy
     2	
     3	Relux Proxy currently ships as a native macOS menu bar app that manages one SSH
     4	dynamic SOCKS5 tunnel. It uses the system `/usr/bin/ssh`, so hosts, keys, jump
     5	hosts, and other options from `~/.ssh/config` continue to work. The planned
     6	versioned contract for saved, concurrent legacy SOCKS tunnels is
     7	[`.spec/legacy-socks-multi-tunnel.md`](.spec/legacy-socks-multi-tunnel.md); it
     8	is not shipped behavior yet.
     9	
    10	The repository also contains the approved specifications and implementation
    11	backlog for a future macOS/iOS system VPN over SSH. That VPN is not implemented
    12	yet. Start with [the specification index](.spec/README.md),
    13	[the current-state inventory](docs/current-state.md), and
    14	[the saved task-board workflow](docs/project-management.md).
    15	
    16	## Use
    17	
    18	1. Open Relux Proxy from Applications.
    19	2. Enter an SSH-reachable IP address, hostname, or `~/.ssh/config` alias, an
    20	   optional account, and a local SOCKS port. Leave **Account** empty to let
    21	   system OpenSSH use the matching config's `User` (or its normal default). A
    22	   non-empty account is an explicit SSH user override.
    23	3. Choose **Connect**.
    24	4. In Firefox, open **Settings → Network Settings**, select **Manual proxy configuration**, and set:
    25	   - SOCKS Host: `127.0.0.1`
    26	   - Port: the port shown by Relux Proxy (`1080` by default)
    27	   - SOCKS v5
    28	   - Proxy DNS when using SOCKS v5
    29	
    30	The initial defaults are `administrator@relux` and `127.0.0.1:1080`.
    31	
    32	## Download
    33	
    34	The latest signed and notarized build always has the same asset name and URL
    35	(GitHub authentication is required while this repository is private):
    36	
    37	https://github.com/relux-works/relux-proxy/releases/latest/download/ReluxProxy.dmg
    38	
    39	Versioned DMGs and SHA-256 checksums are available on the GitHub Releases page.
    40	
    41	## Development
    42	
    43	Requirements: macOS 14 or newer and Xcode 15.3 or newer.
    44	
    45	```bash
    46	make test
    47	make app
    48	make run
    49	```
    50	
    51	### Development tools
    52	
    53	| Command | Purpose | Output or effect |
    54	| --- | --- | --- |
    55	| `make test` | Run the SwiftPM test suite. | SwiftPM build and test data in `.build/`. |
    56	| `make app` | Build and sign the macOS application. | `dist/ReluxProxy.app`. |
    57	| `make dmg` | Build the app, then package a disk image. | `dist/ReluxProxy-v<version>-universal.dmg`. |
    58	| `make run` | Build the app, then open it. | Opens `dist/ReluxProxy.app`. |
    59	
    60	The app is intentionally not sandboxed because it needs to launch the system SSH executable. Release bundles use the hardened runtime and are signed with the Relux Works Developer ID.
    61	
    62	Contributors must follow [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md). Planned VPN work is
    63	tracked in `.task-board/`; no VPN implementation should begin without explicit
    64	approval of the generated plan.
    65	
    66	## Release
    67	
    68	Push a semantic version tag to build, sign, notarize, staple, attest, and publish both versioned and stable-name DMGs:
    69	
    70	```bash
    71	git tag -s v0.1.0 -m "Relux Proxy v0.1.0"
    72	git push origin v0.1.0
    73	```
    74	
    75	The release workflow expects `MACOS_CERT_P12`, `ASC_KEY_ID`, `ASC_ISSUER_ID`, and `ASC_KEY_P8` repository secrets. `ASC_KEY_P8` and `MACOS_CERT_P12` are base64 encoded.
