     1	# Resources
     2	
     3	Resources are linked to board elements via explicit CRUD operations. They are stored centrally in `.task-board/.resources/` (local) or in MinIO / filesystem storage (remote board-server).
     4	
     5	## Resource Types
     6	
     7	| Type | Purpose | Example |
     8	|------|---------|---------|
     9	| **precondition** | Inputs needed before work starts | Design docs, specs, instructions, API schemas |
    10	| **outcome** | Results produced by work | Research findings, implementation notes, analysis |
    11	
    12	## Commands
    13	
    14	```bash
    15	# Create a resource
    16	task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260218-abc, name=TASK-260218-abc_design.md, type=precondition, content="...", description="Architecture design")'
    17	task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260218-abc, name=TASK-260218-abc_results.md, type=outcome, content="...", description="Research findings")'
    18	
    19	# Replace an existing resource
    20	task-board m 'update_resource(TASK-260218-abc, name=TASK-260218-abc_results.md, type=outcome, content="revised findings", description="Research findings v2")'
    21	task-board resource update TASK-260218-abc ./TASK-260218-abc_results.md --type outcome
    22	
    23	# Delete a resource (destructive — requires --confirm)
    24	task-board m --confirm 'delete_resource(TASK-260218-abc, name=TASK-260218-abc_design.md)'
    25	task-board resource delete TASK-260218-abc TASK-260218-abc_design.md --confirm
    26	
    27	# View resources on an element
    28	task-board q --format compact 'get(TASK-260218-abc) { preconditionResources outcomeResources }'
    29	```
    30	
    31	## Storage
    32	
    33	Resources are stored flat in `.task-board/.resources/<elementID>/<name>`:
    34	
    35	```
    36	.task-board/.resources/
    37	├── TASK-260203-g7h8i9/
    38	│   ├── design.md           # precondition
    39	│   └── results.md          # outcome
    40	└── STORY-260203-d4e5f6/
    41	    └── research.md         # outcome
    42	```
    43	
    44	Local and board-server filesystem element deletion is journaled and
    45	crash-recoverable. Direct resource CRUD first resolves any pending staged
    46	element delete under the board mutation lock. MinIO element/subtree deletion
    47	currently fails before mutation with the typed
    48	`ErrAtomicResourceDeleteUnsupported` capability error; ordinary resource CRUD
    49	remains available.
    50	
    51	References are tracked in `progress.md` as markdown links:
    52	```markdown
    53	## Precondition Resources
    54	- [design.md](board-resource://TASK-260203-g7h8i9/precondition/design.md) — Architecture design
    55	
    56	## Outcome Resources
    57	- [results.md](board-resource://TASK-260203-g7h8i9/outcome/results.md) — Research findings
    58	```
    59	
    60	## Spawn Integration
    61	
    62	Precondition resources are automatically injected into agent prompts by `task-board spawn`. Full prompts preserve normal text inlining. Lite prompts use the resolved `agent_context.prompt.preconditions` policy: by default, text below `inline_bytes` is rendered inline, while larger text and binary resources are written read-only under `.temp/resources/` and represented by their name, description, byte count, SHA-256 digest, and local path. This means:
    63	
    64	1. Attach instructions/specs as precondition resources to a task
    65	2. Run `task-board spawn TASK-XX --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-sol --reasoning-effort max` — agent gets everything automatically
    66	3. Agent saves results via `task-board m 'add_resource(..., type=outcome)'` on first write, then `update_resource(...)` for revisions
    67	
    68	## Best Practices
    69	
    70	- **Use preconditions for agent instructions** — attach design docs, specs, or step-by-step instructions before spawning
    71	- **Use outcomes for work products** — research findings, analysis, implementation notes
    72	- **Use explicit create/update/delete** — `add_resource` / `resource add` must not silently overwrite; use `update_resource` / `resource update` when replacing an existing payload
    73	- **Use one safe filename component** — element IDs and resource names containing traversal segments, absolute paths, path separators, malformed URL escapes, or encoded/repeatedly encoded escapes are rejected in local and remote storage
    74	- **Always use board commands** — never create/edit resource files or progress.md resource sections manually
    75	- **Name descriptively with task scope** — `TASK-260218-abc_architecture-design.md` not `doc.md`
    76	- **Add descriptions** — the `description=` param adds a one-line description shown in spawn prompts
    77	
    78	---
    79	
    80	# Bugs
    81	
    82	Bugs are elements of the board, living inside stories alongside tasks.
    83	
    84	```bash
    85	# Create bug
    86	task-board m 'create(type=bug, parent=STORY-260218-abc, name=crash-on-start, description="App crashes when starting recording")'
    87	
    88	# Track like any element
    89	task-board m 'set_status(BUG-260218-abc, status=development)'
    90	task-board m 'add_checklist_item(BUG-260218-abc, text="Reproduce the issue")'
    91	task-board m 'add_checklist_item(BUG-260218-abc, text="Find root cause")'
    92	task-board m 'add_checklist_item(BUG-260218-abc, text="Write fix")'
    93	task-board m 'add_checklist_item(BUG-260218-abc, text="Add regression test")'
    94	```

